Warped clips as Segno plays them (docs/design/audio-editor.md §15, §22, ADR 0063).

A clip that follows the tempo plays past its edges as an unwarped one does (EngineBehaviour's
getAudioClipExtension, for crossfades): its beat range widened, its offset in beats moved to match.
And the behaviour can play an audio clip's source with a node of its own
(createAudioClipSourceNode): Segno's piece player plays warped clips, each piece between warp
markers (or transients, in its Beats mode) read from its own start at its own speed. The clip's
plugins and fades follow that node as they would the engine's.

